      },
      "original_proposition": "[Music] controls. In the bottom right, we have voicing, which if set to mono, only allows one note to be played at a time. useful for bass sounds, for example, when we don't want overlapping notes. When mono is switched off, our synth is polyonic, and the maximum number of notes we can play is customizable. If you're having issues with Serum demanding too much of your CPU, limiting this voice number can be a useful way to remedy this. Finally, we have Portimento, which lets us control pitch glide from note to note. [Music]",
      "knowledge_type": "EXAMPLE",
      "epistemic_status": "SOURCE_REPORTED",
      "normalized_proposition": "controls. In the bottom right, we have voicing, which if set to mono, only allows one note to be played at a time. useful for bass sounds, for example, when we don't want overlapping notes. When mono is switched off, our synth is polyonic, and the maximum number of notes we can play is customizable. If you're having issues with Serum demanding too much of your CPU, limiting this voice number can be a useful way to remedy this. Finally, we have Portimento, which lets us control pitch glide from note to note.",
